<p>Here’s the problem: You are traveling in a different time zone from the <a href="https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/emacs/Emacs-Server.html">Emacs server</a> instance you are accessing remotely via <code>ssh</code> + <code>emacsclient</code>. All clock calculations in that Emacs session are using the local timezone relative to where the server is located. But what you really want is <code>emacsclient</code> to use the current timezone you are in, so things like the mode line clock render accordingly.</p>
<p>To adjust the timezone in an Emacs session, use the command <code>setenv</code> to set the environment variable <code>TZ</code> with a timezone defined in the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tz_database">zoneinfo database</a>. This can be called from Elisp as shown below.</p>
<div class="highlight"><table class="highlighttable"><tr><td class="linenos"><div class="linenodiv"><pre><span class="normal">1</span></pre></div></td><td class="code"><div><pre><span></span><code><span class="p">(</span><span class="nv">setenv</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="s">&quot;TZ&quot;</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="s">&quot;Asia/Seoul&quot;</span><span class="p">)</span>
</code></pre></div></td></tr></table></div>

<p>The latest <a href="https://github.com/kickingvegas/casual/discussions/521">v3.1.0 update</a> of <a href="https://github.com/kickingvegas/casual">Casual</a> adds the command <a href="https://kickingvegas.github.io/casual/Set-TZ.html"> <code>casual-timezone-set-tz</code> </a> that provides a completion interface for selecting a timezone to pass to <code>setenv</code>.</p>
<div class="highlight"><table class="highlighttable"><tr><td class="linenos"><div class="linenodiv"><pre><span class="normal">1</span></pre></div></td><td class="code"><div><pre><span></span><code>M-x casual-timezone-set-tz RET
</code></pre></div></td></tr></table></div>

<p>Note that setting <code>TZ</code> impacts the Emacs session globally; any other running behavior depending on a clock should be taken into account.</p>